// Tool Explorer -- the tri CLI and the MCP servers, each read from its spec.
//
// The fifth step of the site's ladder: Specs → Skills → Crons → Agents → Tools →
// Functions (t27 specs/tools/README.md says "Layer 5"; so does specs/functions). A tool is
// a clap variant of gHashTag/t27 `tri` or an MCP server registered in either
// repository; its card is generated by scripts/agents-from-specs.mjs from
// specs/tools/{tri,mcp}/<name>.t27 through the real compiler. The text on a
// card came from the program it describes (clap `///` doc comments, MCP
// manifests and tool descriptions) and the card names how: `source-parse` when
// read from the source, `help-output` when diffed against `tri --help`. Nothing
// here is typed twice: the commands, their actions, the servers' tools, the
// letters that own them and the counts in the ladder all come from the
// generated catalog, and a tool nobody owns says so.

